\subsection{Tracing the Source Image}

While for duplicated images we suspect that they are generally copied, for several of the images, we could validate and find a source.
Sources were traced by Google Lens search, by targeting search to e-commerce websites and through visual inspection of images associated with the website categories. 

As we could narrow down the search of the source to handful number of websites, some images were recognized even without duplications, such as the generated image shown in first row of \cref{tab:reconstruction-examples}. For this reason, we then continued to visually inspect the generated images comparing them to the original images in the origin websites, under their product categories, leading to exposing of more such memorized images.

