\section{Results}\label{sec:results}


All of our experiments  were conducted on a single RTX A6000 Machine. We primarily focused on Stable Diffusion version 1.4 from the official checkpoint accessible at HuggingFace \cite{SD14HuggingFace}, which is the model where previous attacks were introduced \cite{carlini2023,webster2023,somepalli2023b}. Results from more recent models are discussed and reported in \cref{ssec:other_models}.

In \Cref{fig:clique_examples} we demonstrate examples of four cliques we identified in four different collocations. Since, we generate the cliques using CLIP embedding and not $\ell_2$ distance, notice that in the curtain example cliques may include slightly zoomed-in versions of the same image.  On the other hand, some of the duplicates (e.g. the rugs) can differ only in the color of the rug (that is being segmented and masked for clique identification), while others may involve differing patterns (for example, the wall tapestries).


