The results are shown in Table~\ref{tab:mlpm_200MHz}. The designs are synthesized with Vitis HLS 2023.2 and Vivado 2023.2, with a target clock frequency set to 200 MHz and a target II of 1. The delay constraint is set to 2 for each optimized CMVM operation. Marginal resource savings are observed for these designs for LUTs. However, the designs without \texttt{da4ml} failed to be fully pipelined with an II of 1, and the achieved $\mathrm{F}_\mathrm{max}$ is significantly lower than the target 200 MHz clock frequency. % Due to synthesis time consideration, the CMVM operations in MLP1, MLP2, and MLP3 are only generated once, instead of using explicitly different kernels as the input bitwdiths change. This effectively reduces the lines of generated code by $\mathcal{10}$ times, and the synthesis time after this is around 17 hours on an Intel Core i7-13700K CPU with sufficient memory.

