    \item[$\bullet$] \textbf{$R^2$ Score}: $= 1$.
\end{itemize}

As shown, the model predicts $\varepsilon$ with high accuracy across all modulus sizes. The $R^2$ scores are consistently close to 1. indicating that the linear regression model explains most of the variance in $\varepsilon$ for each modulus size.
