In this section, we demonstrate PathDB's interface and usage. We showcase how to load data into memory, perform path queries, and interact with the system's components. Additionally, we provide a comparison with base methods such as Depth-First Search (DFS) and Breadth-First Search (BFS) with an automaton to illustrate PathDB's capabilities. PathDB is available on GitHub\footnote{\url{https://github.com/dbgutalca/PathDB}}.


%En esta sección se describirá brevemente la interfaz, se describira en breve el conjunto de datos utilziado, algunas consultas de demostración y su equivalencias. 


\paragraph{Dataset}

The dataset is a property graph depicted in Figure \ref{fig:basicgraph}, which represents a fragment of the graph supplied by the LDBC SNB \cite{SzarnyasWSSBWZB22}. This graph comprises two types of nodes, labeled as \code{Person} and \code{Message}, along with three types of edges, labeled as \code{Knows}, \code{Likes}, and \code{HasCreator}.
A notable feature of this graph is its ability to support recursive operations, attributed to the presence of cycles. Specifically, the graph includes an inner cycle formed by \code{Knows} edges and an outer cycle that traverses the concatenation of \code{Likes} and \code{HasCreator} edges.

