\section{Conclusion}
\label{Conclusion}

HERA and Rubato are CKKS-compatible HHE schemes that reduce the communication overhead in transmitting the ciphertext, and achieve higher performance and lower energy compared to the traditional HE. We developed hardware accelerator for HERA and Rubato. We leverage the transposition-invariance property in MRMC function, and improve latency and throughput by vectorization, function overlapping, and bubble elimination. We decouple the RNG and stream key generation phases to hide the latency of sampling random constant. Our design achieve 6× improvement in throughput for both HERA and Rubato and achieve 5×, 3× latency reduction in Rubato and HERA respectively. We also show that Rubato outperforms HERA when implemented in hardware in both performance and area.


