			\parindent=0cm 
			\textbf{Updating DP table:} Using bottom up recursive computation, we have  $D[v_x,d_{v_x}]$ and $D[\bar{v_x},d_{v_x}]$ for each child $v_x$ of $u$ for $1\leq x\leq d_u$. Now, we compute $D[u, j]$ in $j^{th}$ iteration for $1\leq j\leq d_u$, where $D[u, j-1]$ and $D[\bar{u}, j-1]$ are already computed in $(j-1)^{th}$ iteration. Initially we set $D[u,j]=\emptyset$ and update $D[u,j]$ to $D[u,j]\cup\{(w_1+w_2,\alpha_1+\alpha_2)\}$ for each pair $(w_1, \alpha_1) \in D[v_j,d_{v_j}]\cup D[\bar{v_j},d_{v_j}]$ and each pair $(w_2, \alpha_2) \in D[u,j-1]$ (See, figure \ref{fig:t1}). Then, we remove dominated and duplicated pairs from $D[u,j]$. This process executes for each value of $j=1$ to $d_u$. And finally we get $D[u,d_u]$.

