This paper presents both hardness and non-hardness results on power graphs, along with recognition algorithms for specific group classes. Except for the result on $p$-groups in \Cref{sec: motif}, all results in \Cref{sec : non-hardness} and \ref{sec: motif} are representation-independent. For $p$-groups, however, the \textsc{Graph Motif} problem must be treated as a promise problem under standard representation or require algebraic input.

