% The proof of the above lemma works by executing two main steps as follows:
 (1) Given a $3$-SAT formula ${\Phi}$, with $n$ variables, we construct an instance $(\GG,M)$ of \textsc{Graph Motif} in a vertex-coloured graph $\GG$ in polynomial time such that $\Phi$ is satisfiable if and only if $M$ occurs in $\GG$.\\
 (2) We embed $\GG$ as an \emph{induced subgraph} in $Pow(\ZZ_N)$, where $N=n^{O(\log(\log n))}$.%the power graph of a cyclic group of order $n^{O(\log(\log n))}$.

% These two steps are established in \Cref{sat to star-clique} and \Cref{sat to star-clique}, respectively. %*****Why these two steps are enough? here or at the end?*************
