We are now ready to prove \Cref{Graph motif not in P}.

\begin{proofof}{\Cref{Graph motif not in P}}
        The proof is by contradiction. %The exponential time hypothesis is that $3$-SAT with $n$ variables cannot be solved in $2^{o(n)}$ time. 
    Assume that \textsc{Graph Motif} in the power graph of the cyclic group of order $N$ can be solved in $2^{O((\log N)^c)}$ time. Given an instance $\Phi$ $3$-SAT with $n$ variables, using the reduction stated in \Cref{sat to pow}, we get an instance of \textsc{Graph Motif} in the power graph $Pow(\mathbb{Z}_N)$ such that $N=2^{O(\log n \log(\log n))}$. Since $2^{O((\log n)^c (\log(\log n)^c)}=2^{o(n)}$, there is an algorithm of $\Phi$ with runtime $2^{o(n)}$, which contradicts ETH. Hence, our assumption is wrong. \hfill$\blacktriangleleft$
\end{proofof}

