The next theorem follows as a consequence of   \Cref{enumerating abelian p-groups in poly} and \Cref{pow(nil) reducible to dpow(p)}. Subsequently, \Cref{summary} for abelian groups follows directly.

\medskip 

\begin{theorem}\label{recognition abelian}
There is a polynomial time algorithm that takes a reduced directed graph $\Gamma$ as input and recognises whether $\Gamma$ is isomorphic to the reduced directed power graph of an abelian group.
\end{theorem}

