\textbf{Adversary’s Capacity:} We assume that the attacker can access the testing workloads $W_{Test}$ and their results $\mathcal{R}es$. Furthermore, the attacker is capable of performing projection and group-by operations on $\mathcal{R}{es}$ to obtain the joint weights $w_{ij}$ of each tuple $t_i$ in table $R_{x}$ that participates in the testing query $\mathbf{q}_j$. Additionally, 
we assume that the attacker can execute at most $K$ update operations $\Delta D$ (insertions/deletions) on a specific relation $R_x$ within the training database, poisoning the training data into $D' =D+\Delta D$. \looseness=-1


