In this section, we will take a different perspective to transform the seemingly impossible black-box ACA problem from the previous section into a constrained integer nonlinear programming problem that can be tackled. Specifically, we are inspired by the experimental results of learned CE studies~\cite{yang2019deep,nec,ALECE,AreWeReady4CE,DBMSCE}, which show that existing learned estimators possess extremely high estimation accuracy, with their estimates on the training database approaching oracle-level. Therefore, we utilize an oracle estimator $E_{O}$ on the dataset \( D' \) as our surrogate model. We assume that the $E_{O}$ trained on \( D' \) can precisely report the actual cardinality of queries in \( D' \). For $E_{O}$, we have \(  {est}(\mathbf{q}|E_{O}) = C_{D'}(\mathbf{q})  \). Thus, our task now is to maximize the Qerror of the oracle trained on $D'$:\looseness=-1

% LXL: 大MAX 冒号统一


{\small
\begin{align}
& \text{Max}:  \sum_{j=1}^{M}   \max\left( \frac{{est}(\mathbf{q}_j|E_{O})}{C_D(\mathbf{q}_j)}, \frac{C_D(\mathbf{q}_j)}{{est}(\mathbf{q}_j|E_{O})} \right) = \sum_{j=1}^{M}   \max\left( \frac{C_{D'}(\mathbf{q}_j)}{C_D(\mathbf{q}_j)}, \frac{C_D(\mathbf{q}_j)}{C_{D'}(\mathbf{q}_j)} \right) \\
    & \text{s.t. } (1) D' = D + \Delta D \quad (2)   |\Delta D| \leq K\notag\\\notag    
\end{align}}

\vspace{-1em}





