    % We will construct a polynomial-time reduction as follows, transforming instances that only consider deletions into instances that simultaneously consider insertions and deletions. For a database instance of Theorem 4.1, we will create a new instance by multiplying the tuples in $R_x$ by the size of the entire database $|D|$. This ensures that the benefits from insertions are much smaller than those from deletions. The optimal solution to the problem remains the same as the optimal solution considering only deletions. Consequently, we have established a polynomial-time reduction from Theorem 4.1 to Theorem 4.2. Thus, the problem of simultaneously considering insertions and deletions remains NP-Hard.

\end{proof}

